By way of derogation from the requirements set out above, heavy-duty vehicles and electric non-road mobile machinery shall be subject to the following Union origin requirements:
(a) the cab of the vehicle or machinery is manufactured in the Union;
(b) the vehicle or machinery is assembled in the Union;
(c) the ratio between the ex-works price of the components, excluding the battery, originating in the Union and the ex-works price of all components, excluding the battery, is at least 75%;
(ca) at least 80% of the ex-works price of the vehicle or machinery, excluding the battery, corresponds to Union value added. For the purposes of this point, research and development, design and engineering activities, including related intellectual property, royalties and licence fees, shall be considered as originating in the Union only where they are carried out in the Union;
(d) the vehicle's or machinery's traction battery contains the binders and at least three main specific components of batteries, among which the battery cells originating in the Union;
(e) the vehicle's or machinery's traction battery contains the binders and at least five main specific components of batteries, among which the battery cells, the cathode active material (including calcination and active material formation) and the battery management system, originating in the Union;
(f) the ratio between the ex-works price of the electric powertrain components originating in the Union and the ex-works price of all such components is at least 50%.
(g) the vehicle’s traction battery contains at least 20% of precursor cathode active materials (including battery-grade transition-metal precursor compounds), and at least 10% of anode active materials, originating in the Union;
